  "grammarTip": "Real conditions use ako + present tense in both clauses, with the main clause often in the future: 'Ako imam vremena, doći ću' (If I have time, I'll come). Unreal or hypothetical conditions use the conditional mood (bih/bi/bismo/biste + l-participle) in both clauses, typically introduced by kad bi(h): 'Kad bih imao više novca, kupio bih kuću' (If I had more money, I would buy a house).",
